
  
  

<p>The Adam Freeland Song “We Want Your Soul” was released in 2003, and while the world was going through a transitory period, we are realizing the entirety of the soul sucking nature of modernity today.</p>
<p>This version of the music video includes some of the more iconic advertisements of the 20th century, including the Coca-cola ad that is famously the outro of the television show Mad Men. You’ll notice the glazed over looks of the people singing in the advertisement as if they are brainwashed by Coke - which I am sure with modern corn syrup, aspertame, and other ingredients aid in.</p>
<p>The world always wanted your soul, for it is the one thing that you are that does not die. This is a reminder that you don’t have to play the game that the Devil wants you to play, that you can spit in his face, turn your back on him, and look to the coming of our Lord and Savior, Jesus Christ.</p>
<p>As always, God bless, and until next time.</p>
